    "parent": "root",
    "text": "I've paused after 1 minute because while that site you showed looks beautiful, you have to wonder if it is actually functional. Just yesterday I saw a video that was talking exactly about this: that with AI a lot of designers are making beautiful sites but those sites are completely dysfunctional. Like you can't actually immediately see what the site is about and who it is for. He also quoted this research paper that showed that sites that were clear and pragmatic had MUCH higher conversion than super visual designed ones. So be careful: overdesigning can really, really cost you.",
